**Day 43: Introduction to Python Flask**  

**Topic:**  
Flask is a lightweight Python web framework used to build web applications quickly and efficiently. Today covers Flask installation, creating a basic "Hello World" app, and running it locally.  

**Learning Objectives:**  
• Understand what Flask is and its role in web development.  
• Install Flask and set up a development environment.  
• Create a simple Flask application with routes.  
• Run the application locally and view it in a browser.  

**Activities / Deliverables:**  
• Install Flask using pip.  
• Build a basic Flask app with a "Hello World" route.  
• Extend the app to include 3 different routes.  
• Test the app locally using the Flask development server.  

**Important Concepts:**  
• **Routing:** Mapping URLs to Python functions.  
• **Development Server:** Built-in server for testing Flask apps.  
• **WSGI:** Web Server Gateway Interface (Flask follows this standard).  

**SQL Syntax / Commands:**  
• Not applicable for this Flask-focused session.  

**Real-world Use Cases:**  
• Building RESTful APIs for web/mobile apps.  
• Creating lightweight microservices.  
• Prototyping web applications quickly.  

**Tools / Tech:**  
• Python 3  
• Flask  
• VS Code (or any code editor)  

**Summary:**  
Learned the basics of Flask, installed it, and created a simple web app with multiple routes. Practiced running the app locally and understood Flask's role in web development.  

